<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Wanjiku was asked to find <m>{4}\mathbf{a} - {3}\mathbf{b}</m>, where <m>\mathbf{a} = {5 \mathbf{i}+6 \mathbf{j}+4 \mathbf{k}}</m> and <m>\mathbf{b} = {-2 \mathbf{i}-5 \mathbf{j}-4 \mathbf{k}}</m>. Her working has one mistake.</p><ul><li>Step 1: <m>\mathbf{a} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} 5 \\ 6 \\ 4 \end{array}\right)}</m>, <m>\mathbf{b} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} -2 \\ -5 \\ -4 \end{array}\right)}</m></li><li>Step 2: <m>{4}\mathbf{a} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} 20 \\ 6 \\ 4 \end{array}\right)}</m></li><li>Step 3: <m>{3}\mathbf{b} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} -6 \\ -15 \\ -12 \end{array}\right)}</m></li><li>Step 4: <m>{4}\mathbf{a} - {3}\mathbf{b} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} 26 \\ 21 \\ 16 \end{array}\right)}</m></li><li>Step 5: So <m>{4}\mathbf{a} - {3}\mathbf{b} = {26 \mathbf{i}+21 \mathbf{j}+16 \mathbf{k}}</m>.</li></ul><p>(a) Which step has the mistake?</p><div>[ Step 1 | Step 2 | Step 3 | Step 4 | Step 5 ]  </div><p>(b) Give the correct value of <m>{4}\mathbf{a} - {3}\mathbf{b}</m> in i, j, k form.</p><div><fillin characters="15" name="ans2"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) Step 2 is wrong: a scalar multiplies every component, so <m>{4}\mathbf{a} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} 20 \\ 24 \\ 16 \end{array}\right)}</m>.</p><p>(b) <m>{4}\mathbf{a} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} 20 \\ 24 \\ 16 \end{array}\right)}</m>, <m>{3}\mathbf{b} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} -6 \\ -15 \\ -12 \end{array}\right)}</m>, so <m>{4}\mathbf{a} - {3}\mathbf{b} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} 26 \\ 39 \\ 28 \end{array}\right)} = {26 \mathbf{i}+39 \mathbf{j}+28 \mathbf{k}}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p>Step 2</p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>26 \mathbf{i}+39 \mathbf{j}+28 \mathbf{k}</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>